==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Madame Sumo''' at Level 10.

Evolves into '''Riceball Cat''' when obtained from [[Sumo Awakens!]] (may drop on the 1st stage but guaranteed on the 2nd) and is at level 20.

==Strategy/Usage==
A somewhat stronger version of [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cat]], with a faster attack rate and higher health. Very useful in the early game as a resilient unit to protect your long-ranged units, but he will eventually be replaced by Eraser Cat and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cat]] due to their lower cost for what they do. He is also part of many good [[Cat Combo]]s, as explained in the section below.

==='''True Form'''===
Riceball Cat greatly increases his speed (becoming faster than Crazed Wall) and gains immunity to knockback. This gives him some use in some [[Restriction Stage]]s, including [[Cats of the Cosmos]] and {{4c}} Legend Stages, [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 30|Floor 30]] of the [[Heavenly Tower]] and the [[Mega Menace]] stages. He is recommended in stages that grant large amounts of money, but will usually not be worth his cost otherwise, acting like a replacement for Manic Mohawk but with four times the cost.

==='''Talents'''===
Hyper-maxing him and unlocking his health [[Talents|Talent]] solves the low health issue, allowing Riceball Cat to be used almost everywhere as a meatshield. Adding the immunity talents makes him especially useful in stages with enemies that Slow, Freeze, Knockback or use Toxic attacks on cats, as the Erasers would be made less effective by said abilities.

''Note: Start with the health talent and commit to level him up as much as possible first, as his immunities, especially to toxic, will be wasted if the cat itself can't survive the attacks. With this being said, in most Uncanny Legends stages, he will die regardless, so assess your priorities carefully.''

The Attack Buff talent brings nothing to this unit having low base attack power, so avoid it. It also prevents Riceball from stalling or cheesing stages. Use a Talented Riceball Cat with [[Li'l Tank Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Eraser Cat]] for an ultimate defense against [[Henry]]. After completing [[An Ancient Curse]], Riceball Cat can be upgraded up to level 50, which combined with Talents gives him more health than even a level 20+90 Eraser Cat or level 50 Manic Eraser Cat (29,160 > 26,700/25,545).

Riceball Cat should still never be picked over [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]], unless his immunities, naturally low cooldown or speed are required.

Notably, these Talents compete with:
*[[Li'l Tank Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Eraser Cat]] (Immune to Freeze)
*[[Viking Cat (Rare Cat)|Maximum the Fighter]] (Slow Immunity, Talented)
*[[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]] (Slow Immunity)
*[[Vega Cat (Rare Cat)|Vega Cat]] (Toxic Immunity)
*[[Gold Brick Cat (Special Cat)|King Nekokhamen]] (Toxic Immunity)
However, you will most definitely have more mileage out of Riceball's immunities more than the ones mentioned above, aside from Li'l Eraser, Catellite and Green Shell Cat; Maximum lacks bulk and gets frequently juggled, Vega Cat has terrible cooldown and health and King Nekokhamen will die to anything that isn't Floating.

==='''Orb'''===
A Cash Back Ability orb is hard to get, but will drastically improve Riceball Cat's performance as a meatshield. If you happen to have an S-grade orb, it'll reduce his average cost to 225¢. With this orb, he becomes one of the top meatshields in the game, being a Manic Eraser with even faster speed and a wide array of helpful debuff immunities, along with good Cat Combos, for only an extra 75¢, which is a significantly easier price to swallow than without an orb.

